# ============================================================================
# annotate landing revamp — D3 Daylight Margin v2 — FULL PAGE
# Model: nano banana (gemini / gemini-2.5-flash-image) — pinned below.
# AI-GENERATED MEDIA: disclose as AI-generated when published.
# Gate A PASSED 2026-10-18 (user approved D1/D2/D3 generation).
# Copy: design/landing/COPY-v2.md §2 (headline + subhead + CTA pair).
# Run: generate-media-prompt design/landing/prompts/d3-daylight-margin-v2/full-page.media.prompt
# Text budget: 8 strings — the subhead is rendered truncated at its first
#   sentence for render legibility; the full approved subhead lives in
#   COPY-v2 §2. Ticket push is PLANNED: no ticket-creation card anywhere —
#   the roadmap row may carry only a tiny "Soon" chip.
# IA section order (approved): hero → try-it demo band → 7-step walkthrough →
#   features bento → embed snippet → for agents/MCP → roadmap → FAQ → final CTA.
# COPY CORRECTION 2026-10-18 (user): hero secondary CTA is now "Start free"
#   (was "Add to your site"); hero caption and embed heading added; the three
#   embed steps render as bars for text budget (full strings: COPY-v2 §10).
# Build-lane motion notes (not part of the render): 150–200ms ease-out;
#   ring draw-on ~400ms; staggered rail fade. Widget stays dark-on-light
#   (honest dogfood default) or light re-theme via --tobor-kit-* vars —
#   this render stages the dark rail as deliberate contrast per the
#   direction card, but the page itself is paper-light.
# ============================================================================
schema: '0.4'
id: annotate-landing-daylight-margin-v2-fullpage
type: image
quality: high
service: gemini
model: gemini-2.5-flash-image

prompt:
  text: |
    Full-page desktop website mockup, tall portrait, a bright paper-white
    landing page like a well-set document, generous whitespace, one red
    accent. Background #FAFAF8, ink #17171C, hairline borders #E4E4DF. Top:
    slim nav, serif wordmark reading exactly "annotate", four small gray
    nav-link bars, one
    red-filled button. Hero, subject large and high in the frame, left/right
    split: left column has a small eyebrow bar, the two-line large serif
    headline "Feedback that points at the thing.", a two-line muted subhead
    reading "annotate pins threaded comments to the exact element or text
    they're about." with both words "annotate" and "threaded" spelled
    exactly — the complete sentence, no repeated words, all in plain muted
    gray — a red primary button "Try it on this page" beside an
    outlined button "Start free", plus a one-line small muted caption below
    the buttons reading "No signup to look around. To post or install:
    create an account, add your site, paste your tag."; right side, a large
    flat light
    browser window filling most of the frame width: title bar with three GRAY
    dots, a light app page of gray placeholder bars and card shapes, one
    "Export" button surrounded by a HEAVY crisp red ink ring (3px, confident,
    unmistakable) with a small red pin, a thin red connector line running to
    a WHITE comment rail card that is FLUSH DOCKED against the browser's
    right edge with no gap, containing two rows with small red-tinted circle
    avatars and short comment bars. Below, sections in this exact order,
    separated by hairline borders: a wide live-demo band showing a dashed red
    ring around one page element with a small pill; a single row of exactly
    seven small
    light screenshot thumbnails; a bento grid of six bordered tiles with
    placeholder bars and small line glyphs; a small heading "Add your site,
    get your tag" (spelled exactly) above a wide light code panel holding
    only abstract gray bars of varied widths and indents — zero characters,
    no code — and one small icon-only copy button with no
    text label; a short two-column text row with
    bars; a low roadmap row of small outline chips where exactly one tiny
    chip reads "Soon"; four slim accordion rows of gray bars with one small
    "FAQ" label to their left — the word FAQ appears exactly once; a
    closing
    full-width paper strip with one red button. Generous margins everywhere, no
    dead space above the hero. The ONLY text in the whole image is exactly:
    annotate · Feedback that points at the thing. · annotate pins threaded
    comments to the exact element or text they're about. · Try it on this
    page · Start free · No signup to look around. To post or install: create
    an account, add your site, paste your tag. · Add your site, get your tag ·
    Export · Soon · FAQ. All other copy is abstract
    gray placeholder bars. Elegant serif display for the headline, clean
    grotesque for UI strings, small muted type for the subhead, high
    contrast, crisp, no warped text.
  negative: >-
    garbled glyphs, pseudo-letters, misspelled words, duplicated text, prices,
    dollar signs, currency, any real brand name or logo, URLs, hex codes, hash
    symbols, photographic people or faces, initials in avatars, dark theme,
    heavy shadows, hand-drawn scribbles, more than one red element per region,
    second saturated hue, ticket-creation card, Jira or tracker logo,
    watermark, cluttered spacing, dead empty margins, annoate or anobate
    misspellings of the wordmark, legible or semi-legible code characters,
    the word FAQ repeated on every row, the string Add to your site,
    annocate, annobate, a Roadmap label, garbled text rows
  style: >-
    minimal editorial paper-and-ink, heavy 3px red ink ring #D92D20,
    flush-docked rail, generous whitespace, flat vector UI illustration

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions: {width: 832, height: 1248, aspect_ratio: '2:3'}

requirements:
  subject: light editorial landing page, nav to final strip, hero with
    heavy-ringed element and flush-docked rail, demo band, walkthrough,
    bento, snippet, roadmap, FAQ
  composition: subject fills frame, no dead space above hero, sections in
    approved order (hero, demo band, seven thumbnails, bento, snippet, agents
    row, roadmap, FAQ, strip), rail attached with no gap, red reserved for
    ring, pin and primary CTA
  palette: >-
    paper #FAFAF8, surface #F1F1EE, ink #17171C, secondary #5B5B66, border
    #E4E4DF, markup red #D92D20
  dont: [prices, brand logos, URLs, extra text, faces, dark theme, thin faint
    ring, detached rail, ticket-creation imagery as a shipped step]

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.75
  required_pass: [text_legibility, full_page_structure, rail_flush_docked, ring_weight]
  criteria:
    text_legibility: {weight: 3, description: exact string manifest, crisp, no garbled glyphs}
    full_page_structure: {weight: 3, description: nav, hero with CTAs, demo band, seven
      thumbnails, bento, snippet, agents row, roadmap with Soon chip, FAQ, final strip —
      present, ordered, rail attached}
    rail_flush_docked: {weight: 3, description: rail card attached to the browser edge
      with no visible gap}
    ring_weight: {weight: 3, description: heavy crisp 3px red ring — fails if thin or faint}
  reject_if: [garbled or misspelled text, price or currency symbol, third-party logo,
    dark theme, thin faint ring, visible gap between rail and page edge,
    ticket-creation card shown as shipped]

tags: [marketing, landing-fullpage, annotate, daylight-margin-v2, ai-generated]
product_targets: [annotate.therobotlives.com]
